<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yugoslav Committee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1915–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yugoslav Committee was a political body of South Slav exiles from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, formally founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1915 and led by the Croatian politician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ante-trumbic">Ante Trumbić</a>. It lobbied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> for the union of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, and in 1917 signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corfu-declaration">Corfu Declaration</a> with the Serbian government. It took part in creating the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yugoslav-committee.jpg" alt="Yugoslav Committee" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yugoslav_Committee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
